== Notes ==
* Using the {{i|Meat Cleaver}} on Turdlet instantly skips its first phase.
* Since the health Turdlet's split segments have scales depending on how much health the original Turdlet have when it split, if a strong attack (like a {{e|Bomb}} or {{p|II - The High Priestess}}) causes Turdlet to split, its split segments will have significantly less health. 

== Trivia ==
* Turdlet resembles a grounded {{e|Pin}}, albeit with a happier expression.
** Alternatively, it may be a Dross-specific variant of {{e|Larry Jr.}}, seeing as how both bosses slide on the ground.
* Turdlet uses the same scream that the {{e|Gurglings}} and the {{e|Turdlings}} use.
* In the games files, there are unused enemies with the name of "Floater Turdlet" which resemble Drips with the color scheme of Turdlet. This implies that Turdlet may have had another phase or attack planned, but was ultimately scrapped.

